# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in real values as needed.
# Vite only exposes vars prefixed VITE_ to client code — see src/vite-env.d.ts.

# --- Google Drive import (browser-only: no server, no client secret) ------
# Required for the cloud-import "Google Drive" entry to work — without both,
# it still appears in the menu but every action explains what's missing.
# These are build-time values baked into the bundle at `vite build`; they are
# not secrets (there is no client secret in this flow), but a self-hosted
# deployment needs its own, set in *its* build environment. Get these from
# https://console.cloud.google.com/ for a project where you've enabled the
# "Google Picker API" and "Google Drive API":
#   - VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth client ID
#     (Web application), with http://localhost:5173 as an authorized
#     JavaScript origin. Request only the drive.file scope on the consent
#     screen — it's non-sensitive and needs no Google verification.
#   - VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY: APIs & Services > Credentials > API key
#     (restrict it to the Picker API).
#   - VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID: the project *number* (not the project ID) shown on
#     the Cloud console's project settings page. Optional, but recommended.
# See docs/guide/cloud-import.md for the full walkthrough.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
